```console
$ ketch install --help
Install one or more packages

Usage: ketch install [OPTIONS] [PKG]...

Arguments:
  [PKG]...  `owner/repo`, `scheme:id`, `local:<path>`, or a known alias — each may carry `@version`

Options:
      --path <PATH>       Install from a local archive, binary, symlink, or `.app` (sets
                          `local:<PATH>`)
      --name <NAME>       Installed name for a single package (with `--path`, defaults to the file
                          basename)
  -f, --force             Reinstall even when the requested version is already present
      --pre               Consider prereleases when resolving `latest`
      --no-link           Unpack and record the package without putting it on PATH
      --require-checksum  Refuse to install unless the release publishes a checksum
      --asset <NAME>      Use this release asset by exact file name instead of auto-selecting
  -j, --jobs <N>          Packages to work on at once (default: 4, or `jobs` in config.toml)
  -y, --yes               Answer yes to every prompt
      --root <DIR>        ketch root directory (default: ~/.ketch)
  -v, --verbose           Show what ketch is doing, including every request
  -q, --quiet             Only print errors and requested data
      --no-color          Never emit ANSI colour
  -h, --help              Print help
  -V, --version           Print version

```

```console
$ ketch upgrade --help
Upgrade installed packages to their latest release

Usage: ketch upgrade [OPTIONS] [NAME]...

Arguments:
  [NAME]...  Packages to upgrade. Empty means every unpinned package

Options:
      --dry-run     Report what would change without touching anything
      --pre         Consider prereleases
      --force       Upgrade pinned packages too
  -j, --jobs <N>    Packages to work on at once (default: 4, or `jobs` in config.toml)
  -y, --yes         Answer yes to every prompt
      --root <DIR>  ketch root directory (default: ~/.ketch)
  -v, --verbose     Show what ketch is doing, including every request
  -q, --quiet       Only print errors and requested data
      --no-color    Never emit ANSI colour
  -h, --help        Print help
  -V, --version     Print version

```

```console
$ ketch doctor --help
Check the environment and the install tree

Usage: ketch doctor [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --fix         Repair what can be repaired without asking: currently the PATH setup
      --json        Emit JSON instead of text
      --root <DIR>  ketch root directory (default: ~/.ketch)
  -v, --verbose     Show what ketch is doing, including every request
  -q, --quiet       Only print errors and requested data
      --no-color    Never emit ANSI colour
  -h, --help        Print help
  -V, --version     Print version

```

```console
$ ketch registry --help
Compare a package config with the registry's copy before pulling-requesting it

Usage: ketch registry [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  validate  Validate a registry tree (every `ketch.toml`) the way the pre-push hook does
  status    Show the local registry copy's age and source, without fetching
  push      Compare this project's `ketch.toml` with the registry's copy, show the difference, and
            open a pull request with it

Options:
      --root <DIR>  ketch root directory (default: ~/.ketch)
  -v, --verbose     Show what ketch is doing, including every request
  -q, --quiet       Only print errors and requested data
      --no-color    Never emit ANSI colour
  -h, --help        Print help
  -V, --version     Print version

```
